{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1001954-conversion-into-an-epic-storyline","id":1001954,"title":"Conversion into an epic storyline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-11T15:35:42-08:00","id":1001954,"title":"Conversion into an epic storyline","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">I have mentioned that I believe that many of the Admonitoria merits would fit in an epic Changeling game. I thought that I would try my hand at converting some of these merits into some for a pure changeling character. I would love to hear other people\u2019s ideas and suggestions. Although, one merit can be purchased for non-epic characters, it is my hope that this thread will help develop ideas for a Changeling 2e epic storyline.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Enchanting Beauty(2 to 3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Striking looks, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> Your Looks are beyond striking, you are the very incarnation of beauty and eroticism. Or you are the personification of ideal heroism from which villains cringe in terror and the common folk look at in awe. In the two dot version of this merit, your character can buy dots in striking looks up to their wyrd and with the exception of wound penalties, you character is immune to all penalties on appearance (they don\u2019t have bad B.O., they don\u2019t need to spend hours in from of the mirror grooming themselves, and they can walk though a puddle of mud and not get a speck of dirt on their clothes or shoes). At three dots all rolls in which striking looks apply gain the rote quality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>Note: If your character has the fairest seeming, they don\u2019t need striking looks to purchase this merit. If the fairest character does not have striking looks, upon purchasing this merit, they automatically gain the two dot version of striking looks. If the fairest already has the striking looks, they gain twice the normal limit.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Drawback:</i></b> the character is extremely memorable. all other characters gain two dice to notice and recall the character.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Terrifying Beauty(3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Prerequisite:</i></b> Enchanting Beauty, wyrd 10</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Effect: </i></b>Your beauty is now alien and monstrous. Mortals will fall instantly in love (or at least lust) or kill themselves, knowing that they will never be able to match/ compare. When dealing with mortals/human all difficulties in presence and relevant skill drop to zero. If the character is a changeling, if their will power does not match the presence + skill roll, must spend a dot of glamor to try to resist it. If the character with this merit succeeds in their roll, they can cause <i>TWO </i>conditions. If the changeling is a seducer, they can cause the swoon and wanton conditions or the swoon and infatuated conditions. Or they can cause the inspired and Steadfast condition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Wyrd Skill</i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> (1 to 5)</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite</b>: Skill(1)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> The Changeling binds a skill to his wyrd that he amplifies to super human levels. Add your merit dots to the skill. The skill can be raised one level higher than your word would normally allow. This merit can be bought for several different skills.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Drawback:</b> for each skill you buy this merit for, you automatically gain a negative condition associated with the skill.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:38:51-08:00","id":1002125,"title":"","content":"Here are some of my ideas for playing a more monstrous, epic changeling. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Frightful (3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Intimidation 3, or Striking Looks 2 (Frightening), wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> Changelings find your as frightening as huntsmen, you make children cry, brave men shake in their boots, and women cross the street. Any character you target must subtract one from their resolve and composure rolls. Plus all roles dealing in intimidation gain the rote quality. If your characters has an intimidation of at least 3 AND Striking looks merit, subtract an extra dice from all composure and resolve rolls for every point in the striking looks merit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Drawback:</b> You cause revulsion in the people who deal with you. Maybe shaking your hand feels like touching the hairs of a spider or molting snakeskin. Maybe your smile makes them think of a crocodile before it eats you. You subtract one from all socialize rolls and all socializee rolls add +1 in difficulty.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Living Nightmare (3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Frightful, wyrd 10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>You are the boogieman under children\u2019s beds or in the attic, or the monster that stalks men in the woods. You are the very incarnation of of humanities worst fears. All characters stalked by the changeling gain the spooked condition. When dealing with humans all intimidation rolls are an automatic success. Upon seeing the changeling, the mortal will gouge out their eyes or do some other self destructive action try to escape the changeling. Changelings can do a wyrd+ resolve roll to try to resist the effects. If the Changeling with this merit succeeds in their roll, the target changelings suffers both the insenate and frightened conditions.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:43:41-08:00","id":1002430,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When I looked at the final write up for kiths and seemings, I was disappointed that some of the seeming blessings had been removed (Darkling\u2019s ability to see in the dark, elemental\u2019s immunity to their element, oger\u2019s ability to ignore wound penalties, etc)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">So I though I would try my hand at epic merits which are tied to seeming. These first few are for the Fairest Seeming.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Valore(3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Fairest seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> It was your heroism that earned you your seeming. You convinced your fellow prisoners to throw off the shackles, when a fellow escapee fell, you stood over them fighting off the loyalists and hobgoblins. That heroism has now been amplified to epic proportions. You gain +2 to all resolve and heroic action rolls, even if it takes you higher than what your wyrd would normally allow.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Courtliness(2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Fairest seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect</b>: People comment on your charm, skill, and etiquette. All social difficulties are reduced by 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Honor(3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Fairest seeming, resolve 4, composure 4, wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>You are steady before the most frightening and monstrous of evils. All mundane and supernatural attempts to have the fairest <i>KNOWINGLY (hint! hint!)</i> are an automatic dramatic failure.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Air of Nobility(3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Fairest seeming, Honor merit, wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> Sometimes a hero must unite his followers, allies or even innocent bystanders against a monstrous evil. By spending a point a glamour, the fairest can give everyone he targets the steadfast condition, even if the foe is using an ability against them that would usually cause a breaking point.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The Greater Good(4)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Fairest seeming, Air of Nobility Merit, wyrd 10.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> An <i>Extremely Rare talent, </i>even among high wyrd fairest. The goodness of your heart is so great that it can destroy all evil characters. All characters who are evil by the game masters perspective have their dice pools automatically halved. Also, the fairest attacks do aggravated damage.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T10:42:15-08:00","id":1002556,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Here are some ideas for Epic Darkling Merits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Gaze into the Abyss(3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Darkling Seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> The darkling gazed into some of the darkest corners of the human soul as well as Arcadia. As such, the darkling is immune to all perception penalties in darkness, including supernatural darkness (the one exception being when they are blind folded). They can also see through all illusions plus see ghosts in twilight. No dice roll is needed to activate this power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The Smell of Lies(3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Darkling seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> In their escape, they were betrayed by people they trusted and nearly failed. As such, they swore that they would never be deceived again and taught themselves to pierce through deceptions. They gain the power to smell lies, with different lies having a different scent (lies of infidelity smell sickly sweet, while lies about murder smell like rotting flesh). No dice roll is needed activate this power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cloak of Myst and Shadows(3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Darkling seeming, stealth 4, wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> The darkling can not be detected by supernatural means. Powers like aura reading, telepathy, clairvoyance automatically fail. No dice roll is needed to activate this power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Flowing Like Darkness</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Darkling seeming, wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> The Darkling moves and is as fluid as shadow. At night or in areas where there is -1 perception penalties, the darkling gains +3 to all defense and surprise attack rolls. When characters are not looking for the darkling subtract 3 from perception rolls and when they are looking for the darkling subtract 1 from perception rolls.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T22:18:41-08:00","id":1003252,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Here are merits for playing a beast seeming epic character.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Heart of the Beast (1 to 5)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Beast Seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>This brings the beasts nature to the surface. For every dot in this contract, the character gains one function ing animal feature. This includes fur/pelt, prehensile tail, scales, gills, eyes that can see in the dark, hooves, and the prehensile feet of a monkey.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Calling Out the Greater Beast (1 to 5)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Beast seeming, Heart of Beast, wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> For every dot the Beast gains greater animal features like extra arms or legs, the com pound eyes of an insect or arachnid, the fangs of a cobra or the hypnotic gaze of a serpent, the tentacles of an octopus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Beasts of Legend( 1 to 4)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Beast seeming, calling out the Greater Beast, wyrd 8</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> The Beast is now more legendary fae monster than ordinary animal. Maybe they have the lower body of a centaur, but a more humanoid upper body. Maybe they are skinless and covered with a toxic poison. Maybe the breathe out fire or belch a toxic fume that corrupts whatever it touches or and deals aggravated damage. Maybe they can curse whoever their gaze touches. What ever the feature they are now a TRUE monster of legend.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T12:24:15-08:00","id":1003534,"title":"","content":"Here is another epic merit I hope you find interesting. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><br /> <i>Pure-Heart(3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisiste: </b>wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>The Player must decide if their character is an epic hero or villain. If the character is a hero, they completely refreshes his willpower pool when fulfilling his virtue and a villain completely refreshes his willpower when indulging his vice.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Drawback: </b>Trying to refill your dice pool through the opposite channel if greatly increased. Ignore one success for your vice if a hero or your virtue if you are a villain.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:44:58-08:00","id":1003731,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Here are some merits for epic wizened characters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Our Craft and Talent (2)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b><i>wizened seeming, </i>wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>The Wizened has taken their skill or talents and amplified it to superhuman levels. The player chooses one skill and can do it at one fourth the time it usually takes to complete the project. If the roll is an exceptional success, it only takes one eighth the time</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>The Mechanical Man and Machine Girl (1 to 5)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>wizened seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> For each dot in this merit, the wizened replaces on body part with a functioning mechanical device.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","user":"Madhatter","date":". 11-17-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T15:58:46-08:00","id":1004685,"title":"","content":"Here are some epic oger merits. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Might Makes Right (2)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Oger seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>All strength, brawl, and weaponry rolls are an automatic success at three successes instead of five.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Iron Hide(1 to 5)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Oger seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>For every dot in this merit, the over gets a level of soak.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Blow Back</i>(2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Might Makes Right, wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> When the character makes a successful brawl or weaponry roll, their opponent is sent flying backward. The target suffers lethal damage when landing and extra lethal damage if they hit a barrier. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Retribution will Follow</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Oger Seeming, wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>The Oger tuns all wounds penalties into bonuses and will remain conscious no matter how much damage they take.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Feel the Wrath</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Might Makes Right, Retribution will Follow, wyrd 8</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>All Strength, Brawl, and Weaponry rolls and exceptional successes with a single success and damage by such rolls is increased.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T17:16:43-08:00","id":1005913,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Claire Redfield came up with some ideas for really COOL advanced super natural merits. I thought that I would put them here since they could gives ideas on how to make a changelings kith evolve with Potent Kith. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Medium (Advanced, \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Empathy \u2022\u2022\u2022, Medium \u2022\u2022\u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Effect: </b>When your character performs a ritual to create an Anchor Condition, she may spend a Willpower point to make the Anchor permanent. She may also spend a point of Willpower and make a Presence + Occult roll to destroy a ghost's Anchor, contested by the ghost's Resistance + Rank. Success shatters the ghost's Anchor instantly.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Medium (Epic, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Empathy \u2022\u2022\u2022, Medium (Advanced) \u2022\u2022\u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Effect: </b>The medium has become a lord of ghosts, a beacon of both understanding and power over the restless spirits of the dead. Each dot in this Merit grants the character an honorary Rank among ghosts. She adds this Rank to any rolls she makes to contest the powers of the undead. It also allows her to physically interact with ghostly beings and objects, and her unarmed attacks count as a ghost's Bane if her effective Rank is two or more higher than the ghost's Rank. This works only one way, however; even high-Rank ghosts do not naturally have the ability to touch the medium unless she wills it. Additionally, when she destroys a ghost's last Anchor, the ghost must make a Power + Resistance roll, penalized by the character's honorary Rank. If it fails, an Avernian gateway immediately opens up to claim the ghost.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Drawback: </b>Your character is transformed by such a strong connection to the dead. She suffers a penalty on Social rolls with the living made to charm, carouse, or persuade by friendly means, and on all Animal Ken rolls equal to her dots in this Merit. Normal people instinctively sense the aura of frightful death about her, or perhaps her appearance has changed in some noticeably creepy fashion.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Phantasmal Hand (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Presence \u2022\u2022\u2022, Occult \u2022\u2022, Medium (Epic) \u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">You can summon phantasmal objects and even low-Rank ghosts to aid your actions in battle. At first you can shield yourself in ephemeral Twilight energies, but eventually you can enhance your blows with the life-sapping cold of the grave.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Memories of Dust (\u2022): </b>Add half your Occult (rounded down) to your Defense against Close Range attacks made by living targets, as you pull ghostly objects or nearby ghostly echoes to sap a little of the attack's vital energies. This maneuver relies on your Defense being available, but does not apply during a Dodge.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Grave Shroud (\u2022\u2022): </b>Your body is capable of fading into wraith-like shadow in response to an attack, becoming partially incorporeal like the Twilight state of ghosts. The force of the attack seems to pass through you as though you were but a phantom. You may spend 1 Willpower ignore a number of bashing damage from an attack, or downgrade a number of lethal from a single attack, equal to your dots in this Merit.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Touch of the Grave (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> You may spend a point of Willpower to have your unarmed attacks function at Short Range for a turn. This manifests as phantom skeletal hands and ghostly echoes lashing out at your foes. With each successful attack against a living target, you may choose to do half damage in order to drain a point of Willpower from the victim. If your target has no Willpower remaining, he instead suffers a cumulative -1 penalty per attack to Defense and Initiative as his limbs go cold and numb, leaden with the creeping approach of death.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Drawback: </b>This maneuver is incompatible with any other maneuvers that affect unarmed damage. The character may only inflict her normal bashing damage with Touch of the Grave.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Psychokinesis (Advanced, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Psychokinesis \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Effect: </b>Your character's mastery over fundamental forces has grown to incredible levels. Add her dots in this Merit to Resolve + Occult rolls made to activate a form of Psychokinesis. In addition, when she manifests the elemental force, its starting Size is equal to her dots in this Merit or Resolve, whichever is higher. Once manifested, the character may manipulate a force without spending further Willpower, using her rating in this Merit as automatic successes. Note that continued attacks with this Merit require directing the force at a target, with a Dexterity + Occult roll as an instant action. The target's Defense applies to this roll.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Psychokinesis (Epic, \u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Psychokinesis (Advanced) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Effect: </b>The gods once wielded elemental powers to transform the world. Your power now rivals theirs. With the two-dot version, when your character manifests psychokinetic force, its base Size is equal to (Resolve) x 10. At the four-dot version, the power affects an area with a radius of half the character's Resolve in <i>miles</i>, rather than mere yards. This may cause Extreme Environments at a level equal to this Merit (such as freezing cold or city-scorching firestorms).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Drawback: </b>Using the four-dot version of this ability renders it impossible to shape the unleashed psychokinetic energies on a large scale. She cannot increase or decrease the area of manifestation, nor can she attack directly with it. She can attempt to shape a patch of Size equal to (Resolve) x 10. Use of this level of power is not selective, and the sweeping elemental forces do not distinguish between intended and unintended targets. Everything is collateral damage. Using this ability also causes lethal damage to the user equal to the dots in this Merit.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Laying on Hands (Advanced, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022, Laying on Hands \u2022\u2022\u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Effect: </b>The strength of your healing psychic energy is so great that you can cast out injury and infirmity entirely. You no longer suffer bashing damage when healing minor injuries. For each dot in this Merit, you may ignore up to one point of lethal or aggravated damage your character would take on by healing others per scene. This also applies to diseases and poisons. Subtract the character's dots in this Merit from the severity of any ailment to determine whether or not it will affect her.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}